    "rules": [
      "Rebrickable elements.csv lists at least one element of the part in Rebrickable color 0 (Black); the element ID is the lowest whose design_id equals the part number; all are kept.",
      "Rebrickable colors.csv, LDraw LDConfig.ldr and the BrickLink color guide give the Rebrickable, LEGO and BrickLink names and IDs of Black and its RGB (partcolors join rules 2-4); they equal the lego_black row of part_colors.json.",
      "The Rebrickable part number equals the part ID (elements.csv).",
      "LEGO design IDs are the design_id values of the part's Black elements in elements.csv.",
      "The part ID is the BrickLink item number or one of its alternates (pinned BrickLink page).",
      "The pinned BrickLink page lists Black (BrickLink id 11) among the item's colors.",
      "No part is in kit_31203_inventory.json; BrickLink's item name gives the slot (Tile or Plate) and the plaque's dimensions; every plaque's tile and plate have the same studs.",
      "Every citation id resolves to source.snapshots; SHA-256s are 64 hex characters; dates are YYYY-MM-DD.",
